    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta-info"><strong>Last Updated: January 8, 2026</strong></p>

    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>BrainSPA ("we," "our," or "us") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your data when you use our mobile application.</p>

    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We collect two types of information:</p>

    <h3>A. User-Generated Content (Stored Locally)</h3>
    <p>The following data is stored locally on your device and is not transmitted to our servers unless you explicitly perform a backup action (if available):</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Game progress and high scores</li>
        <li>Psychological test results and assessments</li>
        <li>Personal notes or journals</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>B. Usage & Technical Data (Collected by Third Parties)</h3>
    <p>To improve app stability and user experience, we use third-party services that may collect:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Device Information:</strong> Device model, OS version, and unique device identifiers (e.g., IDFV).</li>
        <li><strong>Usage Data:</strong> Launch times, session duration, and feature interaction.</li>
        <li><strong>Crash Logs:</strong> Information about app crashes and system state at the time of error.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p><strong>Local Data:</strong> To provide the core functionality of the app, such as saving your game levels and generating personal insights.</p>
    <p><strong>Technical Data:</strong> To analyze app performance, fix bugs (via Crashlytics), and understand user engagement trends (via Firebase Analytics).</p>

    <h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>We use the following third-party services. These providers have their own privacy policies addressing how they use such information:</p>
    
    <h3>Google Firebase (Analytics & Crashlytics)</h3>
    <p>We use Firebase to analyze how users interact with BrainSPA and to monitor system stability. Firebase may collect your IP address and device identifiers.</p>
    <p><a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank">Firebase Privacy Policy</a></p>

    <h2>5. Data Storage & Security</h2>
    <p><strong>Personal Data:</strong> Your sensitive personal data (such as mental health test results) remains on your device within the app's sandbox environment using iOS standard storage (UserDefaults, Core Data).</p>
    <p><strong>Data Transfer:</strong> While your personal content remains local, anonymous usage statistics are processed by Firebase servers to help us improve the App.</p>

    <h2>6. Your Rights & Opt-Out</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Access or delete your local data by uninstalling the app.</li>
        <li><strong>Opt-out of Analytics:</strong> You can disable tracking in your iOS device settings (Settings > Privacy > Tracking) or through the app's settings menu if available.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>BrainSPA is not intended for children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.</p>

    <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by updating the "Last Updated" date on this page.</p>

